<title>ZIMBABWE: TABLE - FMB raises interim shr, div up.</title>
<headline>TABLE - FMB raises interim shr, div up.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    176.0	vs     141.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     60.0	vs	50.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		61.3	vs	43.8</p>
<p>    Taxation			22.8	vs	14.4</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	    38.6	vs	29.4</p>
<p>    Attrib profit		 78.6	vs	29.4</p>
<p>    Total income		  97.3	vs	78.7</p>
<p>Div payable: September 23</p>
<p>On register: August 29.</p>
<p>Full name: FMB Holdings Limited.</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the results for the period under review were not comparable with last year as they included a profit of Z$3.8 million earned during the three months from April 1 1997 to June 30 1997 by the Heritage Investment Bank (HIB), soon to be merged with the First Merchant Bank of Zimbabwe. Comparative figures for HIB for the same period last year had not been included.</p>
<p>The group said the merger would initially involve additional costs but the long-term benefits of a wider customer and product base, backed by better skills and technology would enable the bank to maintain its leading position in the market.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
